  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWebsites can be made up out of many different resources, hosted by different providers.\n\nThe page itself might be rendered by a specific server and assets like stylesheets might be served by a separate CDN.\n\nIn such configurations only part of the hosting providers might suffer an outage.\n(As what happend with Cloudflare today)\n\nOften it is possible to host assets in multiple locations but swapping the `href` values for large websites is much more complex.\n\nWeb pages will often have server side cache and invalidating the entire cache to swap the `href` value might do more harm than good.\n\nIdeally there is some mechanism to communicate alternative locations for resources.\n\n-----\n\nThis is somewhat possible today:\n\n```html\n<link\n  rel=\"stylesheet\"\n  href=\"https://cdn.com/style.css\"\n  onerror=\"this.onerror=null;this.href='https://example.com/style.css';\"\n/>\n```\n\nBut this solution is bit gnarly.\n\nA dedicated API/feature would be easier to implement and easier to document/teach",
